 the string a `/risk accuracy` reader receives, never a helper one layer below: three tempdir tests (grown / silent / shrank, the last asserting a shrink does *not* wear the growth wording) plus the `learning_freshness` table. **The round's other two bets both lost and are worth not re-deriving:** `signal_names` really is write-only (the loader never compares it to `SIGNAL_NAMES`, so a **reordering** of the seven signals is undetectable) — but the loader is otherwise well defended, with five validated `WeightsDefect` classes (`NotJson`, `NoWeightsArray`, `WrongLength`, `BadValue`, `SumOutOfRange`) and a once-per-process stderr warning, so an *inserted* eighth signal trips `WrongLength`; and there is no weight floor const because none is needed — `compute_adjusted_weights` adds the default as a prior (`hit_rate + RISK_WEIGHTS[i] * (1.0 + surprise_ratio)`) and then blends `0.7 * RISK_WEIGHTS[i] + 0.3 * raw`, flooring every weight at `~0.7 * RISK_WEIGHTS[i] > 0`, so the self-sustaining zero-weight ratchet cannot occur.
